gs  that are within your comfort zone if  you're in your comfort zone all day long  you hate your life it means that you're  setting tiny goals for yourself that you  know you're going to accomplish and  you're basically just photocopying your  life every day is the same is the same  is the same and it's all inside your  comfort zone that's not why humans are  built to do you want to grow you're a  hero you want to go on a journey you  want to do amazing things you want to  help others also if you want to have  more confidence check out our 254 series  they're free and the link to join is in  the description below surround yourself  with greatness if you want to be more  confident you need to surround yourself  with things that make you feel confident  the people who win work the hardest  because they love what they do  what I'm really helpful for me was to  create an outline in the star rule  number five hate mediocrity to make a  real change you have to hate your life  good is the enemy of great if you're  good you're good it would be nice to  have more but you're not willing to do  the crazy scary painful things that  require to get great because you're good  you need to realize if only for a few  moments that you hate your life you hate  it you're capable of more way more this  is nowhere near this is nowhere near max  you know this is nowhere near the max in  your capabilities you should hate that  you need to hate that and then you make  a powerful decision to change so if  you've ever been to a Tony Robbins  unleash the power with an event the  three and a half day event his most  powerful exercises that he does is his  Dickens exercise and what he has you do  is write down your limiting beliefs he  has he write down what are the things  that that you do that is holding you  back the belief system you have that is  holding you back the things that you  know you need to act on that you're not  doing why is it that you're not doing it  and what does it holding 